1
00:00:00,060 --> 00:00:02,734
In this town, shadows work the night shift.

2
00:00:03,627 --> 00:00:06,604
When we go to sleep, our shadows get up.

3
00:00:07,593 --> 00:00:09,055
They fix the roads.

4
00:00:09,527 --> 00:00:10,686
Clean the streets.

5
00:00:11,327 --> 00:00:12,486
Paint the fences.

6
00:00:13,127 --> 00:00:16,407
That's why our town is always perfect in the morning.

7
00:00:17,493 --> 00:00:19,562
Nobody has ever seen them work.

8
00:00:20,227 --> 00:00:21,992
You're not allowed to look.

9
00:00:22,560 --> 00:00:23,719
Not even once.

10
00:00:24,360 --> 00:00:25,822
But I couldn't sleep.

11
00:00:26,293 --> 00:00:28,362
So I looked out my window.

12
00:00:29,027 --> 00:00:31,701
Hundreds of shadows were working on Main Street.

13
00:00:32,593 --> 00:00:34,055
Tall ones. Small ones.

14
00:00:34,527 --> 00:00:35,989
Mine was there too.

15
00:00:36,460 --> 00:00:38,225
I recognized its messy hair.

16
00:00:38,793 --> 00:00:40,558
It was carrying a ladder.

17
00:00:41,127 --> 00:00:42,286
Then it stopped.

18
00:00:42,927 --> 00:00:44,086
And turned around.

19
00:00:44,727 --> 00:00:46,795
And looked straight at my window.

20
00:00:47,460 --> 00:00:49,225
I hid under my blanket.

21
00:00:49,793 --> 00:00:51,897
In the morning, everything was normal.

22
00:00:52,527 --> 00:00:54,292
Except my shadow was gone.

23
00:00:54,860 --> 00:00:56,625
I stood in the sun.

24
00:00:57,193 --> 00:00:58,655
Nothing on the ground.

25
00:00:59,127 --> 00:01:00,892
I asked my friend Leo.

26
00:01:01,460 --> 00:01:02,922
His shadow was fine.

27
00:01:03,393 --> 00:01:07,583
At school, my teacher pointed at the floor where my shadow should be.

28
00:01:08,993 --> 00:01:10,455
And went very pale.

29
00:01:10,927 --> 00:01:12,389
"It quit," she whispered.

30
00:01:12,860 --> 00:01:15,837
"Shadows only quit when they find a better person."

31
00:01:16,827 --> 00:01:18,895
That night, I followed the shadows.

32
00:01:19,560 --> 00:01:21,022
To the old factory.

33
00:01:21,493 --> 00:01:23,562
Where they sleep during the day.

34
00:01:24,227 --> 00:01:26,295
And there it was. My shadow.

35
00:01:26,960 --> 00:01:28,422
Attached to someone else.

36
00:01:28,893 --> 00:01:31,265
A boy who looked just like me.

37
00:01:32,060 --> 00:01:33,825
Same hoodie. Same messy hair.

38
00:01:34,393 --> 00:01:35,855
He smiled at me.

39
00:01:36,327 --> 00:01:38,395
"Thanks for the shadow," he said.

40
00:01:39,060 --> 00:01:41,734
"Now I just need the rest of you."

